Subject: tests: on OpenVMS, check only that timeout runs a command

Process creation on VMS takes much longer than the 10ms that
require_timeout_ allows, and a firing GNV timeout in a batch job kills
the calling shells as well.  The tests use timeout only as a guard.

--- a/tests/init.cfg	2026-10-03 04:13:32.677864055 +0100
+++ b/tests/init.cfg	2026-10-03 04:13:32.692819201 +0100
@@ -42,8 +42,18 @@
     || skip_ your system lacks the timeout program
   returns_ 1 timeout 10s false \
     || skip_ your system has a non-GNU timeout program
-  returns_ 124 timeout 0.01 sleep 0.02 \
-    || skip_ "'timeout 0.01 sleep 0.02' did not time out"
+  # On OpenVMS, creating the child takes far longer than 10ms, and when
+  # GNV's timeout does fire in a batch job it kills the calling shells too.
+  # The tests use timeout only as a guard that should never fire, so just
+  # check that it runs a command.
+  case $(uname -s 2>/dev/null) in
+    OpenVMS)
+      returns_ 0 timeout 10 true \
+        || skip_ "'timeout 10 true' failed" ;;
+    *)
+      returns_ 124 timeout 0.01 sleep 0.02 \
+        || skip_ "'timeout 0.01 sleep 0.02' did not time out" ;;
+  esac
 }
 
 require_pcre_()
